\title{Writing your own estimator}
\description{
By default the package estimates with \code{mixl}, which is fast and handles both
multinomial and mixed logit. It is not the only thing you might want to fit. The
\code{estimator} argument of \code{\link[=sim_choice]{sim_choice()}} and \code{\link[=sim_all]{sim_all()}} therefore accepts a
function of your own, so you can put any model in the loop while keeping the
simulation, the aggregation and the power calculations as they are.
